# Independent review of Increment C-a

Review the completed diagnostic and proposed architecture against section 10 of docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-08-pit-optimizer-v5-transition.md. The deliverable is a concrete finding or narrow design, not source implementation or a campaign-readiness decision.

Read package-review.diff once, then the evidence paths it identifies where needed. Source lookups are permitted only for concrete provenance/design risks. Review the authority-trace report independently from the principal diagnosis. Verify that per-round saved config identity is a defensible authority anchor, that summaries and component-only evidence are accurately distinguished, and that the proposed boundary preserves live guards/default callers and fails closed on incomplete history.

Binding constraints: no tests read/created/modified/run, synthetic inputs/events/records, credentials/environment values, external requests, evaluation/campaign/Docker operations, production edits, historical writes, commits or Git manipulation. Do not rerun the one-shot summary scripts. Use only saved real evidence, source/AST/hash reads. Do not delegate. Write only independent-review.md in this package.

Return two verdicts: spec compliance and diagnostic/design quality. Cite file/line for actionable findings and source checks. Evaluate the package's acknowledged incorrect initial cross-encoding comparison and its corrected superseding evidence; do not treat either a claimed correction or a report assertion as proven without inspecting evidence. Identify any unresolved component or trust assumption that is misstated. No broad rereview of accepted B4c or unrelated dirty branch work.

This is the sole full-package review for this read-only increment, including the delegated authority task. The package contains added artifacts rather than new commits; base and HEAD remain a068e0aed40ecbe5e0078924071f374e7809b8c2. The diff explicitly covers only newly authored documentation and diagnostics.
